 ## Authentication and database troubleshooting
 
-FunctionGram uses email/password sign-up and sign-in only, with email verification required. No social authentication providers are configured. Passwords must be 12–128 characters. Password recovery is supported end to end: `POST /api/auth/request-password-reset` emails a single-use link valid for 15 minutes (Brevo, same send limits as verification), the link opens `/reset-password`, and a successful reset revokes all existing sessions. All of it is covered by the E2E tests in `tests/auth.test.ts`.
+FunctionGram uses email/password sign-up and sign-in only, with email verification required. No social authentication providers are configured. Passwords must be 12–128 characters. Password recovery is supported end to end: `POST /api/auth/request-password-reset` emails a single-use link valid for 15 minutes (Brevo, same send limits as verification), the link opens `/reset-password`, and a successful reset revokes all existing sessions. Admin and moderator access additionally requires verified TOTP/recovery-code 2FA, an absolute 12-hour session, and a database-verified role. `/rstmcadmin/security` documents the owner/admin/moderator permission matrix; only owners grant or revoke roles. The configured bootstrap account remains `admin`; designate the first `owner` explicitly through a reviewed out-of-band database operation—never infer it from the bootstrap email or preview account. `/rstmcadmin/audit` is an append-only, filtered viewer with bounded CSV export. `ADMIN_IP_ALLOWLIST` optionally accepts comma-separated IPv4/IPv6 addresses or CIDRs; leave it empty to disable, and configure only confirmed owner/operator networks. New admin device fingerprints trigger an audit event and a rate-limited email notice without persisting the raw fingerprint tuple. All of it is covered by the E2E tests in `tests/auth.test.ts` and `tests/admin.test.ts`.
 
 Set the Production `DATABASE_URL` to the active Neon production branch. Set Preview to a separate Neon branch before testing. A successful build does not verify a database connection; check `/api/health` after deployment. If `POSTGRES_URL` is also present, it takes precedence and must point to the intended database. Environment changes require a new deployment. Never commit connection strings or auth secrets.
 
